HEAD: b86b7ce

==========================================================================
S2a  THE RUN
==========================================================================
  population: the 422 CANDIDATE STEPS of S1d
  Each is run ONCE, from its own tree, with its transcript holding the
  committed bytes, under an `open` audit hook.  Output goes to memory --
  NOTHING in the subject tree is rewritten by this sweep -- and the tree
  is `git checkout`-restored after every single probe.

  timeout per probe: 120 s.  A probe that does not finish is recorded as
  TIMEOUT and is neither counted as biting nor as clean, because a probe
  that did not run has not answered the question.

  workers: 4.  THIS PASS TRUNCATES NOTHING -- every run here has its
  transcript populated -- so concurrent workers cannot empty a file out
  from under each other.  S3, which does truncate, runs SERIALLY.

      ...STEPS run                                                  422
          ^ one unit of that number is one step
      ...STEPS that TIMED OUT at 120s                                40
          ^ one unit of that number is one step
      ...STEPS that exited non-zero                                 101
          ^ one unit of that number is one step

  THE TIMEOUTS ARE A CEILING ON WHAT THIS PASS COULD SEE, AND THEY ARE
  STATED HERE RATHER THAN AT THE BOTTOM.  A probe killed at 120s may not
  have reached the line that opens its own transcript, so it is recorded
  as not-reading when the truth is not-known.  Every count below is
  therefore a LOWER BOUND over the 422 steps, exact only over the 382 that
  finished.  The arc's own runners take ten minutes in places; this
  suite runs 422 probes and cannot give each of them ten.

==========================================================================
S2b  THE EMPTIED CLASS -- THE ONE THIS TICKET IS ABOUT
==========================================================================
  population: the 422 STEPS run in S2a
      ...STEPS whose probe OPENS ITS OWN emptied transcript          37
          ^ one unit of that number is one step
      ...STEPS whose probe opens ANOTHER transcript (STALE, not empty)     13
          ^ one unit of that number is one step
      ...STEPS whose probe opens no transcript of its tree          372
          ^ one unit of that number is one step

      ...STEPS whose probe WRITES its own transcript itself           0
          ^ one unit of that number is one step

  THAT ROW IS PRINTED EVEN THOUGH IT IS 0.  A probe that writes its own
  transcript opens EXACTLY THE SAME PATH as one that reads it, and an
  `open`-event hook that ignores the mode counts both.  The first
  version of this pass did.  So the distinction is a REAL correctness
  fix whose MEASURED EFFECT HERE IS 0, and both halves of that sentence
  are load-bearing: the fix is right, and it changed nothing, and
  reporting it as though it had rescued a count would be attributing a
  repair to evidence that does not support it.

  AND WHAT PROMPTED THE FIX WAS A DIFFERENT DEFECT.  Two transcripts
  came out of an early pass MODIFIED, and the first explanation reached
  for was `their own probes write them`.  It was not: they were written
  by probes of OTHER trees, which this suite's timeout had killed before
  their cleanup `finally` could run.  A rigorous fix, a confident
  mechanism, and the mechanism was wrong.  S6/SD3a and SD6c keep both.

      ...RUNNERS with at least one EMPTIED step                      21
          ^ one unit of that number is one `run_all.sh`
      ...further RUNNERS with only STALE steps                       11
          ^ one unit of that number is one `run_all.sh`

  mg-03d1 reports 43 trees where 'a probe of the same run reads a
  transcript that run HAS ALREADY EMPTIED'.  Under its own rule the
  reading probe need not be the one whose transcript was emptied, so
  its 43 covers BOTH classes above.  Mine at the tree grain, and by
  observed opens rather than source text:

      EMPTIED trees   21
      + STALE-only    11
      = both classes  32      (mg-03d1's rule, my measurement)

  I DO NOT GET 43 EITHER WAY, and the reason is the rule and not the
  arc.  The number that answers the ticket's own sentence -- a probe
  reading a file THE SAME RUN EMPTIED -- is 21 trees / 37 steps.

